# Source: https://github.com/samtools/samtools/issues/142
# Symptom: fields are separated by multiple consecutive spaces rather than
#   exactly one space or a tab; samtools view treats each space as a delimiter,
#   so two consecutive spaces produce an empty field between them, causing the
#   parser to interpret the remaining fields in the wrong positions.  With
#   double space "17 1  105", samtools count differs from the correct value.
#   BED should use a single tab as field separator (the de facto standard,
#   despite some legacy tools accepting whitespace).
17  1  105
17  200  300  feature001
